---
title: Shader includes & defines
description: Preprocess reusable WGSL chunks and typed compile-time constants.
order: 10
sidebar:
  label: "Shader Includes & Defines"
---

Material and `PingPongShaderPass` fragments share a preprocessor for named includes and defines. Preprocessing happens before contract validation and WGSL compilation, while retaining a generated-to-source line map.

## Includes

Declare source chunks in the material and reference them from a line containing only the directive:

```ts
const material = defineMaterial({
	fragment: `
#include <math>
fn frag(uv: vec2f) -> vec4f {
	return vec4f(remap(uv.x, 0.0, 1.0), uv.y, 0.0, 1.0);
}
`,
	includes: {
		math: `fn remap(x: f32, a: f32, b: f32) -> f32 { return (x - a) / (b - a); }`
	}
});
```

Include names must be WGSL-safe identifiers. Included chunks may include other chunks recursively. Unknown names, empty source, invalid directives, and circular chains throw before shader compilation; circular errors include the expansion stack.

Expansion replaces directives recursively and records the original fragment or include line for every generated line.

## Defines

Defines are sorted by name and emitted as top-level WGSL `const` declarations before the expanded fragment.

| Input | Emitted type |
| --- | --- |
| `boolean` | `bool` |
| Unwrapped number | `f32` |
| `{ type: 'bool' &#124; 'f32' &#124; 'i32' &#124; 'u32', value }` | Explicit scalar |
| `{ type: 'vec2f' &#124; 'vec3f' &#124; 'vec4f', value }` | Explicit float vector |

```ts
defines: {
	ENABLE_GLOW: true,
	ITERATIONS: { type: 'i32', value: 8 },
	TINT: { type: 'vec3f', value: [1, 0.65, 0.35] }
}
```

Numeric components must be finite. Integer defines require integers, `u32` cannot be negative, and vector tuple length must match its type.

## Defines or uniforms

Use a define when the value is part of compiled shader structure, such as a feature flag, loop bound, or static vector constant. Use a uniform for runtime data. Changing a define requires a new material and changes the material signature; changing a uniform value updates the existing buffer.

## Diagnostics

The line map labels compilation failures as fragment, include, or define locations. `PingPongShaderPass.setFragment(fragment, { defines, includes })` uses the same preprocessing and replaces its pipeline only after the new source passes contract validation.
